WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.170
- Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.340
My next guest is a
four-time Grammy-winning

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.030
recording artist, that's
four, okay, who encouraged

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.460
all the independent women out
there to put their hands up.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.410
Now she's a mom, has new
music and she's on a mission

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.460
to raise awareness about how hard

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.640
the African-American community
has been hit by COVID-19.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.120
Let's say hi to Kelly Rowland

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:19.953
What's up, Kelly?

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.750
- Hello, Kelly.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.630
I love that--

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.640
- I love you, first of all,
I love your song "Kelly".

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.560
I jam to it all the time.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.470
- Thank you

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.380
- I mean, obviously, I love
your song, "Kelly", obviously,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.900
but I'm just it's I love that song.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.270
I'm trying to figure out a
way to cover it on my show

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.430
without looking stupid but I
love, I just love that song,

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.100
It's so great but I do want to get to why

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.590
you wanna talk here today.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.580
It's important to me as well.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.850
Actually my house manager,
one of my really good friends,

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.110
Ava, we've been talking about
this because she's in LA

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.850
holding our house down for
us and I'm like don't go out

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.310
because it's worse for African-Americans

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.780
and where are you right
now and how is quarantine

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:56.850
going for you though?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.320
- The quarantine is going
good and you're actually

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.410
absolutely spot on right, Kelly.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.410
It's funny when you start
to think about the ratio

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.030
and population of black
people, we only make up 13%,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.070
which, of course, makes us minority

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:16.070
but it's 33% of COVID
patients are African-American,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.840
and some of them were African-American,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.570
because of course, you
know, the virus comes

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:22.410
and it's so many different
types, and I don't,

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:25.770
it's just so mind-blowing,
but 30 that's a big number

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.530
33% of patients are African-American,

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.470
and we have to get that
number down and I don't know

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.830
what's making people feel
like either it can't happen

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.870
to them whether they're in
African-American community

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.310
or not, but you have
to take this seriously

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:43.840
because one thing happens
like right after another,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.550
which is oh, you go
out, your friend has it,

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.400
your friend gives it to
you, you give it to grandma,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.820
then auntie, then this person,
then those people give it

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:53.800
to someone else.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.560
That's how it spreads so
fast and we just have to take

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.150
this way more serious
and you gotta think about

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:04.840
also the the illnesses
from high blood pressure,

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:08.040
high cholesterol, hypertension, asthma,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.750
so many different illnesses that have been

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.970
really generational, illnesses in

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.330
the African-American community.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.210
- And if you have those, getting
COVID makes it worse, yeah.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.670
- Yeah, we just wanna
be smart about all this

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.300
and I just really wanna encourage
everyone to stay inside.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.010
We're not quite done
with this but we can be

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.090
if we really practice our
social distancing and have,

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.470
I like to say kindness, because
when you actually approach

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.170
this with kindness, then you'll
think about the fact that

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.060
I don't want this to happen
to me and let me just be kind,

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.740
stay in my home and be
smart about all of this.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.870
- And be kind to others, be
respectful because maybe you

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.349
have an okay immune system
and maybe you might be fine.

00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:57.990
First of all, I do love
a level of invincibility.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.810
People think they're
invincible like, they watch

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.370
and they're like oh that
happens to someone else

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.865
I'm like, you could be that
someone else really quick.

00:03:03.865 --> 00:03:06.860
It's a crazy time right now but,

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.940
in quarantine for me coming
back to your question

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.620
has been nuts because you
know we have three kids

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.740
with us right now, our
18-year-old's in Florida

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.510
but we have a lot of
kids, a lot of homework,

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.580
a lot of cooking, a lot of still working.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.400
Its been a really hard
go, I'm not gonna lie

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.540
there's not a self help book
in the world that could help

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.945
my psyche last week. (laughs)

00:03:25.945 --> 00:03:27.020
- No, not at all.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.020
- How is yours going, is yours nuts?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.210
- It's going good like literally
you could probably hear

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.960
Titan in the back on the Zoom
call with this classroom.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:38.560
- My little Remi is right in
there watching Mickey Mouse so.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.010
- It's real so between that
and he's the only child

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.763
I do wanna have another one so bad

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.690
but he's by himself so
he expects my attention

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.010
at home all the time,

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:52.810
which is sometimes overwhelming
and I still have work to do

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.840
and putting out music and finishing up

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.160
literally finishing up an
album which I'm very excited.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.250
I cannot wait to get out of quarantine.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.960
I'd love to play you some
records but it's just really

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.440
I feel bad for him because
I also had to think about

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.650
the fact that the same way
I'm trying to think about

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.970
all this and like, flushed
all of these thoughts out,

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.950
so is he.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.870
So at like the most
random times of the day,

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:18.130
he'll just act out and then
I'll hone in on him and like,

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.070
look at him and then I know
like play therapy works

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.530
with him so we'll start playing with cars.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.860
And after a while, I'm
like, do you know why

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.660
you got so upset?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.367
And then he'll tell me why and he's like,

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:32.170
"I miss my friends and
I wanna go to school."

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.190
- That's what my kids say.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.760
- Yeah, it's the same so
they're trying to figure out

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.540
what's going on with them
too is just, oh, you have

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:42.048
to have some patience with these babies.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:45.400
- I 100% agree but let's talk about one of

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.240
your other passions and congrats
on your new single "Coffee"

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.510
and then you actually have
an Instagram Live Show,

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:51.720
called Coffee with Kelly?

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.563
- Yes, yes I do.
- I love it!

00:04:54.563 --> 00:04:56.170
I wanna talk about Coffee with Kelly

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:58.310
- We're so naughty on
the show in a good way

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.800
because like you just said
like prior of course to

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.080
like stick shifting
gears, we're all bombarded

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:07.210
with so much Coronavirus
statistics and facts

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:10.390
and new information everyday
to where it kind of soaks up

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.430
everything that we are and consumes us

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.420
and brings forth anxiety and
that's what it was doing to me.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.050
And I was like I have to break this up

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:20.040
so I came up with Coffee with
Kelly and it's just literally

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:23.580
us having like talking sex and
kinky stuff and just have--

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.300
- I love it, I'm in!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.811
- Exactly, its fun!

00:05:26.811 --> 00:05:29.850
So, it definitely brings
a light and we have

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.690
a really good time.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.750
Yesterday we were talking
about relationships

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:36.140
and quarantine and you know,
some people came on like hard.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:42.270
- It is, I keep saying this, I
keep going man, there's a lot

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.990
of babies are gonna come out
of this and a lot of divorces.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.142
(chuckles)

00:05:46.142 --> 00:05:47.170
- It's true.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.480
- It's so hard because we're
always around each other

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.313
all the time.

00:05:50.313 --> 00:05:51.146
I love that though.

00:05:52.145 --> 00:05:54.350
And I don't know if it's a
Kelly thing but I love the fact

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.060
that you are very open or a Texas thing

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.140
but, you're very open and
Rowland, really, I mean

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:01.673
you know, you're like, oh,
we get nasty and I'm like

00:06:01.673 --> 00:06:04.910
Sex ain't nasty, everybody
has sex, everybody does--

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:07.050
- Yeah, everybody does have sex.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.270
- It's like you notice
the way you, approach

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.440
all those subjects and
I think it's awesome.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.510
And I think it's really important to have

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.570
not just stiff content and
I think it's, you know,

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.890
to have real raw content,
just real conversations.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.310
I think it's cool, so congratulations
on that, it's awesome.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.583
- Thank you so much.

00:06:23.462 --> 00:06:25.660
- I've always been a fan,
I'm such a big fan of you

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.470
but I just want to say thank
you and I want everybody

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.630
to check out Kelly's new
show, Coffee with Kelly

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:32.450
on Instagram, as well as
her new single, "Coffee".

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.550
Y'all better get that.

